required packages
- open3d 
  - requires
      - python 3.11
- numpy
- torch
  - image model dependency MiDaS
    - timm (pip install timm)
    - midas' transform assumes a normalised numpy data type for the current verrsions, so u have to manually change pil image data type to normalised (0,1) numpy array
- cv2

| Library             | Role                                                                                          |
| ------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **cv2 (OpenCV)**    | Handles camera input and image manipulation.                                                  |
| **torch (PyTorch)** | Runs the MiDaS neural network for depth prediction.                                           |
| **numpy**           | Handles numerical math, grids, and array reshaping.                                           |
| **open3d**          | Used to represent and visualize 3D geometry (point clouds, meshes).                           |
| **PIL (Pillow)**    | Simplifies image conversions (used to convert OpenCV frames into the format PyTorch expects). |

the computational power required to run my goal is not availiable, so a sugested downscale is to have a static render that recaptures say every 10 seconds and added any new object to the space 